<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F3.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A3</span>: </span><span id="S5.F3.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative comparison of depth prediction for six frames (first three frames are <span id="S5.F3.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span>, the future three frames are <span id="S5.F3.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">red</span>. LFG is able to decouple static and dynamic objects as it continues along the road, and future work will improve the sharpness of the last frames’ predictions.
<span id="S5.F3.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dashed red</span> outlines denote predicted frames with <em id="S5.F3.9.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no ground-truth image input</em>, produced solely from the model’s future tokens.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
