<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A6</span>: </span><span id="S6.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">More qualitative comparison of motion predictions (LFG vs Pseudo) with corresponding RGB frames. In this scene, LFG predicts the moving car across the intersection, but also the close pedestrians, demonstrating that the pretrained point decoders of <math id="S6.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> improve the predictions.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
